#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hypr Settings — a click-and-pick control panel for Hyprland.

Runs in a floating kitty window. Navigate with mouse clicks or
arrow keys / Tab / Enter — no search bar anywhere.

Design: sidebar navigation + titled cards, colored with the live wallust
palette. The app background stays the terminal's default color (ansi_color
mode), so kitty's slight transparency shows through — glass, like the rest
of the desktop.

Appearance changes apply LIVE via `hyprctl keyword`; the Save button
writes them into ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf so they survive reboot.
"""

